  "term": "exotropia",
  "definition": "Exotropia is a type of eye misalignment in which the eyes’ visual axes point outward instead of aligning properly. It can happen when the inward-pulling muscle is weak, leaving the outward-pulling muscle relatively unopposed so the affected eye turns laterally.",
